If you've ever tried to get into ComfyUI, you know the drill. You download a workflow, half the nodes are missing, you're hunting down custom node packs, something's incompatible with your GPU, and hours later you still haven't made a single image. That barrier keeps most people out of local AI generation entirely, especially if you're running an older card or something under 12GB of VRAM.

This video is sponsored by SimpliGen, a desktop app that turns that whole mess into a simple wizard. Pick what you want to make, pick a style, describe it, generate. No node graphs, no dependency hunting, and a built in cloud option if your hardware can't handle local generation. I walk through the app, the character consistency system, local versus cloud generation, and then plug in my own LoRAs to build consistent AI influencer content with it.

